From: Pavankumar Nandeshwar <pnandesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2025 21:14:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: read PPE MEC status from the HTT overlay

Firmware completions use an HTT status overlay on the WBM descriptor.
Reading HTT status bits from the WBM info0 word instead interprets the
TQM release reason as an HTT status.  That can either miss a MEC
notification or discard a real PPE completion, leaving its direct-switch
buffer incorrectly owned.

Cast the descriptor to the HTT overlay before filtering MEC notifications.
Its leading reserved words already account for the status offset, matching
the final QSDK layout after its HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET cleanup.

Based-on: 27de30f7c1e9832d82d6ef03adf0aed8fee3a513
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0531-UPSTREAM-DP-wifi-ath12k-Remove-the-usage-of-HTT_TX_W.patch
Signed-off-by: Pavankumar Nandeshwar <pnandesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -797,6 +797,7 @@ int ath12k_ppe_ds_service_tx_completion(
 	struct ath12k_ppe_ds *ppe = &ab->dp.ppe_ds;
 	struct ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc *tx_desc;
 	LIST_HEAD(completed);
+	struct htt_tx_wbm_completion *status_desc;
 	struct hal_wbm_completion_ring_tx *desc;
 	struct hal_srng *srng;
 	u64 addr;
@@ -815,9 +816,12 @@ int ath12k_ppe_ds_service_tx_completion(
 		if (le32_get_bits(desc->info0,
 				  HAL_WBM_COMPL_TX_INFO0_REL_SRC_MODULE) ==
-					  HAL_WBM_REL_SRC_MODULE_FW &&
-		    le32_get_bits(desc->info0, HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_INFO0_STATUS) ==
-					  HAL_WBM_REL_HTT_TX_COMP_STATUS_MEC_NOTIFY)
-			goto next;
+					  HAL_WBM_REL_SRC_MODULE_FW) {
+			status_desc = (struct htt_tx_wbm_completion *)desc;
+			if (le32_get_bits(status_desc->info0,
+					  HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_INFO0_STATUS) ==
+			    HAL_WBM_REL_HTT_TX_COMP_STATUS_MEC_NOTIFY)
+				goto next;
+		}
 		if (le32_get_bits(desc->info0, HAL_WBM_COMPL_TX_INFO0_CC_DONE)) {
 			addr = le32_to_cpu(desc->buf_va_lo) |
 			       (u64)le32_to_cpu(desc->buf_va_hi) << 32;
-- 
